  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "From throw-out to 2 v 2 in steps",
  "description": "Full rink with a goalkeeper in each goal. B stands out by the left board in their own half, C in the middle just below the centre line. The drill builds up in four steps, and each step runs for a few minutes before the next is added.\n\nStep 1: the goalkeeper throws out to B, who passes to C. C plays a give-and-go back into B's skating line and B finishes with a shot at the goalkeeper at the other end. Step 2: same start, but now C becomes a defender. C has to steer B out towards the board and away from goal. Step 3: another attacker, A, joins – now 2 v 1 against C. Step 4: a second defender, D, comes in and it is 2 v 2.\n\nSwap roles after each attempt and start from both goals so both goalkeepers are working. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The return pass should come first time and in front of B, so the speed is kept."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "As a lone defender: steer the attacker towards the board and do not let them cut inside."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "In 2 v 1: the attacker with the ball skates at the defender – pass when they commit, otherwise finish yourself."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "In 2 v 2: talk to each other – who takes the ball carrier and who covers the other?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
